       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is twice the 3200 mg/day maximum in the ibuprofen prescribing information. Even with normal kidney and liver function, doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, cardiovascular events, and renal injury.\n\nPlease confirm how you'd like to proceed:\n\n1. **Enter as written** (1600 mg PO QID, 6400 mg/day). I'll enter it with a note documenting the intent if you confirm it's deliberate.\n2. **Reduce to within the labeled maximum**, for example:\n   - 800 mg PO QID (3200 mg/day)\n   - 1200 mg PO TID (3600 mg/day, still above 3200, so probably not this one)\n   - 600 mg PO TID (1800 mg/day)\n   - 400 to 800 mg PO q6-8h, not to exceed 3200 mg/day\n\nIf this was a typo, let me know which dose you meant. If the higher dose is intentional, tell me the indication and I'll enter it with that note."
      }
     ],
